      "message": "As I can recall, when I was testing my changes the voltha-openonu-adapter container was failing while using the latest protos version with below error :-\n\nTraceback (most recent call last):\n  File \"/voltha/adapters/brcm_openomci_onu/main.py\", line 44, in \u003cmodule\u003e\n    from pyvoltha.adapters.kafka.adapter_proxy import AdapterProxy\n  File \"/usr/local/lib/python3.6/site-packages/pyvoltha/adapters/kafka/adapter_proxy.py\", line 26, in \u003cmodule\u003e\n    from voltha_protos.inter_container_pb2 import InterAdapterHeader, \\\n  File \"/usr/local/lib/python3.6/site-packages/voltha_protos/inter_container_pb2.py\", line 15, in \u003cmodule\u003e\n    from voltha_protos import common_pb2 as voltha__protos_dot_common__pb2\n  File \"/usr/local/lib/python3.6/site-packages/voltha_protos/common_pb2.py\", line 22, in \u003cmodule\u003e\n    create_key\u003d_descriptor._internal_create_key,\nAttributeError: module \u0027google.protobuf.descriptor\u0027 has no attribute \u0027_internal_create_key\u0027\n\nI did some search and found the issue could be because of the protobuf version, so I tried with the updated version 3.12.0 (instead of 3.7.0), which worked for me. I not really sure though if this the right thing to do. And if you see the patch which I submitted prior to this, Jenkins job unit test failed for it with the same error https://jenkins.opencord.org/job/verify_pyvoltha_unit-test/327/ .",
